## Finding Schema

{% set _v = config.reviewers.verbosity | default("standard") %}
{% set _kind = reviewer_kind | default("") %}
Common envelope (every finding):

- `severity`: `"P0"` | `"P1"`{% if _v != "terse" %} | `"P2"`{% endif %}{% if _v == "full" %} | `"P3"`{% endif %}
- `file`: relative path
- `line`: 1-indexed line, or `0` for whole-file
- `summary`: ≤ 80 chars; what is wrong
- `suggestion`: ≤ 200 chars; concrete fix
{% if _v != "terse" %}
- `reasoning`: 4-step Observe→Trace→Infer→Conclude (P0/P1 only)
{% endif %}
{% if _v == "full" %}
- `rationale`: 1-2 sentences; why this severity rather than one notch lower
{% endif %}
{% if _kind == "security" %}
- `category`: `"secrets"` | `"injection"` | `"auth"` | `"permissions"` | `"dependency"` | `"prompt-injection"`
- `evidence`: the offending code excerpt (≤ 200 chars)
{% elif _kind == "performance" %}
- `expected_impact`: quantified when possible (e.g. `"50% fewer allocs"`, `"O(n²)→O(n)"`)
{% elif _kind == "concurrency" %}
- `race_kind`: `"data-race"` | `"deadlock"` | `"isr-blocking"` | `"dropped-future"` | `"ordering"`
- `evidence`: the offending code excerpt (≤ 200 chars)
{% elif _kind == "ux" %}
- `wcag_ref`: e.g. `"WCAG 2.1 SC 2.4.7"` when an a11y criterion is implicated
{% endif %}

### Worked example

{% if _kind == "security" %}
```json
{
  "severity": "P0",
  "file": "src/auth/login.py",
  "line": 42,
  "category": "secrets",
  "summary": "OAuth client secret embedded in source",
  "evidence": "CLIENT_SECRET = \"sk-prod-abc123\"",
  "suggestion": "Move to env var; rotate the leaked value before merge.",
  {% if _v != "terse" %}"reasoning": "Observe: hardcoded literal at line 42. Trace: imported by api/server.py and shipped to clients. Infer: any read of the bundle leaks the prod secret. Conclude: P0 — secret is live and rotation is mandatory.",{% endif %}
}
```
{% elif _kind == "performance" %}
```json
{
  "severity": "P1",
  "file": "src/index/build.py",
  "line": 88,
  "summary": "O(n²) lookup inside hot indexing loop",
  "expected_impact": "100× speedup on 10k-doc corpus",
  "suggestion": "Hoist `for d in docs: x in d` to a precomputed set before the loop.",
  {% if _v != "terse" %}"reasoning": "Observe: nested `in list` at line 88. Trace: called once per document in build_index. Infer: scales as len(docs)². Conclude: P1 — measurable on the existing 10k corpus.",{% endif %}
}
```
{% elif _kind == "concurrency" %}
```json
{
  "severity": "P0",
  "file": "src/cache/store.py",
  "line": 17,
  "race_kind": "data-race",
  "summary": "Shared dict mutated without lock from worker pool",
  "evidence": "self._cache[key] = value  # called from N workers",
  "suggestion": "Wrap with self._lock or switch to threadsafe TTLCache.",
  {% if _v != "terse" %}"reasoning": "Observe: bare dict assignment at line 17. Trace: workers in submit() touch _cache concurrently. Infer: dict resize during write corrupts state. Conclude: P0 — undefined behaviour under load.",{% endif %}
}
```
{% elif _kind == "ux" %}
```json
